# NORMALIZE — the differ's normalization set. CHECKED IN, not code
# folklore: tools/lobo-differential replaces the VALUE of exactly the
# response headers named here with `<normalized>` — on BOTH sides of
# the diff — before comparing. Everything else byte-compares, CRLF
# included. Every future entry needs a comment saying WHY (a differ
# that quietly normalizes is a differ that lies).
Server   # implementation identity: the two servers legitimately differ here forever
Date     # wall clock: legitimately different on every run
@error-footer   # ws41, a BODY rule: a default error page (4xx/5xx, the 416 a Range
                # can draw) ends in the server's identity footer — nginx's token on
                # nginx, lobo's on lobo (the documented body analogue of Server; see
                # serve.error_body). The footer's text and that response's
                # Content-Length are normalized, and the length only when it equals
                # the body's real byte count, so a wrong length still reds.
